Let's find a recursive formula for $g(n)$.

- The first term is the initial size of the collection, which is $\blue{12}$ stamps.
- The common difference is the amount Burak added each week, which is $\pink{4}$ stamps.

Therefore, this is the recursive definition of the sequence:

$\begin{cases}
g(1)=\blue{12}
\\\\
g(n)=g(n-1)+\pink{4}
\end{cases}$

In conclusion, $g$ is an *arithmetic* sequence.

$\begin{cases}
g(1)=\blue{12}
\\\\
g(n)=g(n-1)+\pink{4}
\end{cases}$
